  "evidence": "Original N/E/U shows a sustained ~-19 mm N, +2.5 mm E, -20 mm U offset from day 564 to 584 (P3), with clear return starting at day 585 (P4) and continuing through day 588 (P5), where observations resume near pre-offset levels. P1 (558–560) is an isolated spike without opposing return; P2 (563) is a single-point outlier inconsistent with surrounding motion; P6/P7 (600–601) coincide with a new permanent step (N/E/U jump to ~25/−3/−13), not a return. Only P3–P5 form a coherent temporary platform: onset at 564, return across 585–588, interior stable offset, and physical motion preserved outside. Numerical tool accepts P5 and P6/P7 but visual inspection shows P6/P7 are part of a permanent step, not return.",
